<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Évian Accords</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algerian-war">Algerian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Évian Accords were the agreements signed in 1962 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Algerian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algerian-war">Algerian War</a>. They led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>'s independence that year and marked one of the final chapters in the dismantling of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/evian-accords.jpg" alt="Évian Accords" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UtCon Collection · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%89vian_Accords.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Évian Accords</b> of 18 March 1962 ended the war, a referendum on 1 July approved independence almost unanimously, and Algeria became independent on 5 July 1962.</blockquote><a href="/empire/french-algeria">French Algeria · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Dien Bien Phu in 1954 ended French Indochina; Morocco and Tunisia gained independence in 1956; fourteen sub-Saharan colonies and trust territories became independent in 1960; and the <b>Évian Accords</b> of March 1962 brought Algerian independence after eight years of war.</blockquote><a href="/empire/french-empire">French Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Words and music were officially adopted in 1962, the year in which the <b>Évian Accords</b> were signed and a referendum followed in which Algerians voted overwhelmingly for independence, which was duly granted.</blockquote><a href="/songs/kassaman">Kassaman</a></li></ul></section>
